 loss for fitness preparation", "Urinary β-hCG testing pending as part of workup"], "excluded_candidates": ["Appendicitis: Pain typically localizes to right lower quadrant, less likely to cause hypotension without shock features", "Liver abscess: Could explain RUQ pain and instability, but lacks fever or leukocytosis in this case", "Hepatic rupture from trauma: Unlikely given exercise as precipitant in a non-cirrhotic patient"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension and tachycardia (possible hypovolemic shock)", "Sexual activity without contraception (ectopic pregnancy risk)", "Recent rapid weight loss (potential metabolic stress)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic Pelvic Emergency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.23872679045092837, "posterior": 0.2937916764446769, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic alcohol use and rapid weight loss weakly support hepatic vascular insufficiency as a possible mechanism for RUQ pain and instability."], "evidence_against": ["RUQ pain and lack of amenorrhea weakly contradict ectopic pregnancy (B1) as the primary explanation for acute pain, though hemodynamic instability remains cons…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic Vascular Insufficiency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6445623342175066, "posterior": 0.34754299493051494, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic alcohol use provides stronger support for hepatic vascular insufficiency (B2) compared to gynecologic emergency (B1). Weight loss weakly supports both,…"], "evidence_against